course: dictionary
lesson: 12510
title: Deprived and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deprived means not having enough of the things people need for a good life, such as money, food, a good home or a good school. «The deprived area needed a new school and a park.» The area lacks these things, so deprived describes the place.
explain: Deprived is often followed by of, which means kept from having something. «Mia was deprived of sleep after the loud party.» Mia did not get the sleep she needed. Check by swapping in your meaning: "Mia did not have enough sleep" still makes sense.
explain: Deprived is the past form of the verb deprive. In formal writing, to be deprived of a right means the right was taken away from you. Look for clue words such as of, area, or a need like sleep, food or water.
fact: Deprived means not having enough of what people need for a good life.
fact: «Deprived» is the past form of the verb deprive: deprive, deprives, deprived, depriving.
fact: «Deprived of» means kept from having something, as in «deprived of sleep».
fact: A «deprived area» is a place where people often lack money, good homes or good schools.
fact: Being deprived of sleep or water is dangerous to your health.
exercise: «The village was deprived of clean water for a week.» What does deprived of mean here? | *Kept from having clean water | Painted a bright blue colour | Given lots of clean water | Very close to a river
exercise: Mia was sleep-deprived after the loud party. What does sleep-deprived mean? | *Not getting enough sleep | Sleeping very well all night | Dreaming about parties | Sleeping on a boat
exercise: Which phrase names a place where people often lack money, good homes or good schools? | A quiet holiday | A sunny beach | A busy harbour | *A deprived area
test: In «a deprived childhood», what does deprived mean? | *Not having enough of the things a child needs | Being very tall for your age | Living by the sea | Having a happy and rich childhood
test: Which word is the past form of deprive? | depriving | depriver | *deprived | deprivation
exam: «A deprived area often needs better schools and homes.» Which word tells you the area lacks things? | needs | better | area | *deprived
